%I A217513 #41 Nov 26 2026 09:44:12
%S A217513 2,8,20,32,38,56,74,86,116,130,136,166,190,208,238,264,288,318,342,
%T A217513 360,384,420,444,492,522,534,588,612,648,690,714,732,768,822,840,894,
%U A217513 942,966,1026,1050,1068,1134,1190,1220,1256,1280,1310,1382,1418,1448,1508
%N A217513 Partial sums of nonzero terms in A005926.
%C A217513 Sizes of clusters of atoms in diamond structure.
%C A217513 a(n) is the number of lattice points (X, Y, Z) in the diamond cubic structure (scaled so nearest-neighbor distance is sqrt(3)) within Euclidean distance sqrt(16*n + 3) of a bond midpoint, i.e., a(n) = 2 * #{(x, y, z) in Z^3 : (4*x + 1)^2 + (4*y + 1)^2 + (4*z + 1)^2 <= 16*n + 3 and x + y + z == 0 (mod 2)}. - _Andrew J. Morris_, Nov 21 2026
%H A217513 Andrew J. Morris, <a href="/A217513/b217513.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a> (first 99 terms from Andy Huchala)
%H A217513 Andrew J. Morris, <a href="/A217513/a217513.txt">C++ program</a>
%H A217513 N. J. A. Sloane, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1063/1.527472">Theta series and magic numbers for diamond and certain ionic crystal structures</a>, J. Math. Phys. 28 (1987), 1653-1657.
%F A217513 From _Andrew J. Morris_, Nov 21 2026: (Start)
%F A217513 a(n) = Sum_{k=0..n} A005926(16*k + 3).
%F A217513 G.f.: (psi(sqrt(x))^3 + psi(-sqrt(x))^3) / (1 - x), where psi(x) = Sum_{k>=0} A010054(k)*x^k. (End)
%F A217513 Conjecture: a(n) ~ Pi*(16*n)^(3/2)/48. - _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Nov 26 2026
%e A217513 For n = 0, 16*0 + 3 = 3; the single solution with x + y + z even is (x, y, z) = (0, 0, 0), giving a(0) = 2*1 = 2.
%e A217513 For n = 1, 16*1 + 3 = 19; adding the three permutations of (-1, -1, 0) yields 4 solutions, giving a(1) = 2*4 = 8.
%e A217513 For n = 2, 16*2 + 3 = 35; adding the six permutations of (1, -1, 0) yields 10 solutions, giving a(2) = 2*10 = 20.
%o A217513 (C++) // See links.
%Y A217513 Cf. A005925-A005927, A010054, A217512-A217514.
